            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, an 18-year-old male admitted on 19/11/2023 with a one-day history of periumbilical pain migrating to the right iliac fossa, associated with nausea, low-grade fever, and leukocytosis. Clinical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point. Abdominal ultrasound confirmed the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. Blood tests and vital signs monitoring were performed throughout the stay. The patient underwent a laparoscopic emergency appendectomy on 20/11/2023 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, intravenous fluids and analgesic medication were administered. Wound care was carried out, and the patient recovered well. He was discharged on 22/11/2023 in good general condition with oral analgesia and wound care instructions. Please arrange follow-up in approximately two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me should any concerns arise.</div>"
            },
